win32u, winewayland: windows on, and moved between, screens of different scale

Lightroom Classic on a 100% Cintiq next to a 175% main screen (operator: "The UI scale is totally messed up",
"It launched on my main monitor at 100% scale instead of the 175% it should be"). Lightroom reads its scale once at
launch and ignores WM_DPICHANGED, so on Windows a mixed-dpi desktop gets it right through DPI virtualization (the
"System" high-DPI override: system-aware process, bitmap scaled per monitor). Wine has that machinery; our stack
broke it, and broke maximized windows of every awareness moved between the screens:

- win32u get_surface_rect: crop the window surface against the virtual screen in the THREAD's coordinates, not the
  raw one. A system-aware window on the 96-dpi screen (coordinates 1.75x its pixels) was drawn into 640x1280 of its
  3840x2160. NEUTRON_SURFACE_CROP_DPI=0 restores the old crop.
- win32u set_raw_window_pos: map a driver rect to the app's coordinates through the monitor the window is mostly on
  (map_window_rect_raw_to_virt), as map_window_rects_virt_to_raw does the other way. A maximized window's frame
  overhangs onto the neighbor monitor; its top-left picked the wrong scale, the driver's resize came back 1254x687
  instead of 2194x1202, nothing committed, and a system-aware or dpi-unaware window maximized on the second screen
  never appeared. NEUTRON_RAW_WINDOW_MONITOR=0.
- win32u: a maximized window moved to another monitor by the driver keeps its restore rect on that monitor
  (per-monitor-aware windows; normal_rect follows, scaled to the new work area). NEUTRON_NORMAL_FOLLOWS_MONITOR=0.
- winewayland attach_shm: when the new buffer covers the window, set the viewport destination to the window size.
  Reconfigure runs before the attach and measured the previous buffer; a window moved back to the 175% screen was
  shown at 1317x731 of 2194x1202 until its next paint. NEUTRON_ATTACH_DEST=0.
- winewayland follow_output: record a maximized configure's height for an output only when it belongs to that output
  (fits it, and the surface's preferred scale is that output's). During a move the new output's size was stored, in
  the prefix, under the output being left. NEUTRON_WORKAREA_GUARD=0.
- winewayland: neutron-attach diagnostic (NEUTRON_WL_DIAG=1).

Harness sysmax.c + run-sysmax.sh (KWin's presented buffer vs frame, saved heights), system/pm/unaware x start on
either screen: 140 FAIL 6/6, patched PASS 6/6; each kill switch brings back its own failure.

--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -3119,6 +3119,34 @@
     return rect;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON raw-window-monitor: map a WINDOW rect from MDT_RAW_DPI to MDT_DEFAULT coordinates through the monitor the
+ * window is mostly on, as map_window_rects_virt_to_raw() does the other way. map_rect_raw_to_virt() takes the monitor
+ * under the top-left corner, which for a maximized window is the NEIGHBOR monitor: its frame hangs a few pixels past
+ * the work area. A system-dpi-aware Lightroom maximized on a 100% screen right of a 175% one had its left edge at raw
+ * x=3838, on the 175% screen; a driver resize to 2194x1202 raw was converted there (1:1), applied in place on the 100%
+ * screen and came back to the driver as 1254x687 -- smaller than the compositor's configure, so nothing ever committed
+ * and the window could not be moved. Kill switch NEUTRON_RAW_WINDOW_MONITOR=0. */
+RECT map_window_rect_raw_to_virt( RECT rect, UINT dpi_to )
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    struct monitor *monitor;
+
+    if (on < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_RAW_WINDOW_MONITOR" );
+        on = !e || e[0] != '0';
+        if (!on) ERR( "neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_RAW_WINDOW_MONITOR = 0 (environment)\n" );
+    }
+    if (!on) return map_rect_raw_to_virt( rect, dpi_to );
+
+    if (!lock_display_devices( FALSE )) return rect;
+    if ((monitor = get_monitor_from_rect( rect, MONITOR_DEFAULTTONEAREST, 0, MDT_RAW_DPI )))
+        rect = map_monitor_rect( monitor, rect, 0, MDT_RAW_DPI, dpi_to, MDT_DEFAULT );
+    unlock_display_devices();
+
+    return rect;
+}
+
 /* map a monitor rect from MDT_DEFAULT to MDT_RAW_DPI coordinates */
 RECT map_rect_virt_to_raw( RECT rect, UINT dpi_from )
 {
